1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:01,767
The cloud sounds
harmless, right?

2
00:00:01,967 --> 00:00:04,767
Until a giant data centre
moves next door.

3
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:06,633
Suddenly, it's personal.

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,467
Behind the AI boom

5
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:09,900
are real buildings,

6
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:13,267
using land, power,
and other resources.

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,500
The International
Energy Agency

8
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,333
expects data-centre
electricity use

9
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:19,600
to roughly double

10
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,033
from twenty twenty-five
to twenty thirty.

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,667
So neighbours are asking:

12
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:24,933
can our grid cope?

13
00:00:25,133 --> 00:00:27,533
And who's paying
for those new power lines?

14
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:30,067
Some cooling systems
use water,

15
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:32,233
depending on their
design and location.

16
00:00:32,467 --> 00:00:34,500
In dry regions,
that matters.

17
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:36,467
Others worry about noise

18
00:00:36,467 --> 00:00:39,233
from cooling equipment
and backup generators

19
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:40,267
near their homes.

20
00:00:40,733 --> 00:00:42,700
From Mexico
to South Africa,

21
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:44,900
communities have demanded
clearer answers

22
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,767
about projects
on their doorstep.

23
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:50,467
Of course, data centres
run useful services.

24
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,633
Supporters point to
investment and tax revenue.

25
00:00:53,867 --> 00:00:55,333
Those benefits matter, too.

26
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,067
But so does the deal:

27
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,033
transparent resource use,

28
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:01,633
noise controls, fair costs,

29
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,500
and residents involved
before construction starts.

30
00:01:04,967 --> 00:01:06,667
The cloud may be global.

31
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:07,900
Its neighbours aren't.

32
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:09,967
If the future's
moving next door,

33
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,333
shouldn't they get a say?
